At least some of the color confusion does seem to be intentional:
consider the otherwise completely inexplicable Elvenking on the Plane
of Earth.

That doesn't mean _all_ the devs necessarily consider it a feature; I
rather suspect that it may not have been deliberate at first, but that
later developers took advantage of it since it was there.

Ps. I checked, and it seems monster colors in the modern sense were
introduced in NetHack 3.0.4, released in 1989.  (2.2e and later had
color, but all monsters were colored the same.)  The elemental planes
were introduced in 3.1.0 (1993), and tiles in 3.2.0 (1996).

Curiously, while most "royal" monsters, including dwarf kings, were
purple already in 3.0.4, Elvenkings stayed bright red (the default
monster color in earlier versions) until 3.0.7.  The Wizard of Yendor
has always been purple since 3.0.4, as have mind flayers since their
introduction in 3.1.0.

An interesting detail is that, while dwarf kings and mind flayers have
been the same color in all versions that had both, the colors are not
written the same way in the source: dwarf kings are HI_LORD, while
mind flayers are simply CLR_MAGENTA.  Both map to the same actual
color, though.

